infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Kafka producer throughput: default vs tuned
  desc Same cluster, brokers idle below 20% — only the producer config changed
  compares
    - label Default
      children
        - label Config: linger.ms=0
          desc Kafka 3.x out of the box
        - label 40 MB/s throughput
          desc Capped far below the hardware
        - label Tiny batches, weak compression
          desc One request per send(); codec has nothing to pack
    - label Tuned
      children
        - label Config: linger.ms=20, batch.size=128 KB
          desc Deliberately wait to fill batches
        - label 300 MB/s throughput
          desc 7.5x more on the same cluster
        - label Fat batches, compression 2–4x
          desc Fewer, fatter requests; repetitive logs pack well
theme
  palette #f43f5e #10b981
